Q: I have severe insomnia, which sutras should I recite?
Sources: Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_general,qa_metaphysics
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
I'm sorry you're going through this — not being able to sleep wears down both body and mind. 🙏

Before I suggest a practice for you, let me ask one thing so I don't give you the wrong starting point:

**Have you recited Buddhist sutras before, or is this completely new to you?**

In the meantime, here's what I can share safely:

**If this is new to you — start simple**

Begin with just two:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (Ta Pei Chou)** — 3 times daily
Before reciting, say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], with good health and a peaceful mind."*

📿 **Heart Sutra (Hsin Ching)** — 3 times daily
Before reciting, say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], to open my wisdom, keep my mind clear and calm, and remove my worries."*

**Important timing note for insomnia specifically** — Master Lu taught that the Heart Sutra should be recited **before 10pm**, and not during heavy rain, thunderstorms or lightning. If you feel physically weak, recite it in the daytime on a sunny day. Also avoid reciting anything between 2am and 5am.

So: recite in the daytime or early evening, not right before bed.

If you don't know the words yet, that's fine — you can follow along with the guided recitation videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

**On the medical side**

Heart Dharma Door teaches caring for both body and mind together. Severe insomnia can have medical causes, so please also see a doctor. Recitation works on the spiritual obstacles; the doctor works on the physical side. **Both hands together — that's how you recover fastest.**

Keep reciting steadily, not "for a few days to see if it works." Faith, vow, action — believe first, then practise. Guan Yin Bodhisattva will help you at the right time. 🙏

Let me know your experience level and I can guide you further from there.

═══ CHIP2-en I keep arguing wit — guard: clean ═══
Q: I keep arguing with family, what can I start learning?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 1 (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: introduction,qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Arguing at home is draining — I understand 🙏

Master Lu taught in *Metaphysics Q&A*:

> To a certain extent, interpersonal conflicts are the result of negative karmic ties from your previous lives.

So the way we work on it is not by winning the argument, but by resolving the karmic knot through recitation.

**You can start with this:**

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3 times a day (build up to 7)
Prayer before: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], with good health and strengthened energy."*

📿 **Heart Sutra** — 3 times a day (build up to 7)
Prayer before: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], to gain wisdom, keep a calm and clear mind, and remove my afflictions."*
(Not after 10pm)

📿 **Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots** — 21 to 49 times a day
Prayer before: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me, [your full name], and [family member's full name], to resolve our negative karmic ties."*

📿 **Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance** — start with **1 time a day** (beginners should not do more; add slowly later)
Prayer before: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], to repent and eliminate my karmic obstacles."*
(Not after 10pm)

You can also recite the **Heart Sutra 7 times a day for the family member** you argue with most, praying that Guan Yin Bodhisattva blesses them (say their full name) and grants them wisdom. Master Lu said it's best not to tell them you're doing this.

If you don't know how to recite yet, don't worry — there are follow-along videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Keep going consistently. Don't measure by days — measure by whether you're doing it sincerely. Bodhisattva will help at the right time 🙏

**One question so I can guide you better:** have you recited any of these sutras before, or is this completely new to you?

Reference: *Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3 (Q116, Q127)*

═══ CHIP3-en Work has been goin — guard: passed_after_retry ═══
Q: Work has been going badly, is it karma?
Sources: Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 1 (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: qa_general,qa_metaphysics,introduction
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Work going badly is painful, and it's a very fair question to ask. 🙏

Master Lu's teaching is that when we've created negative karma in past or present lives, it stores in us and shows up in daily life. In *Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 2* he explains it this way:

> The more black energy patches there are on the body, the more unpleasant experiences with health, career and relationships this person would be having .

So yes — career difficulty is often connected to karmic obstacles. But this is good news, not bad news: karma can be reduced. It isn't a fixed sentence.

Here is where to start:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra — 7 times daily**
Before reciting, say:
"Please, Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, bless me, [your full name], with good health and strengthen my spiritual power."

📿 **Heart Sutra — 7 times daily**
Before reciting, say:
"Please, Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, bless me, [your full name], to open my wisdom, keep my mind clear and calm, and remove my worries."
(Not after 10pm.)

📿 **Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance**
Before reciting, say:
"Please, Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, help me, [your full name], to repent and eliminate my karmic obstacles."
(Not after 10pm.)

On the Repentance — please read this carefully. In *Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 2*, Master Lu says the best method to eliminate negative karma is persistently reciting the Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance 7 times per day **together with** reciting Little Houses — 3 to 4 Little Houses per week. That combination is for practitioners with an established practice. If you are just beginning, start with a small number and build up slowly, because the Repentance activates karma and Little Houses are what clear it away.

If you don't know the pronunciation yet, follow along here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Once these are steady, there are also smaller mantras suited specifically to career and wishes — we can look at those later.

Can I ask one thing so I point you the right way: **have you recited before, or is this completely new to you?**

If you'd like someone to sit with you and go through it, or to receive free scripture books, any Heart Dharma Door centre will help — 33 branches nationwide: https://xlfm.my/contact-us 🙏

═══ CHIP4-en My child is rebell — guard: clean ═══
Q: My child is rebellious, how should I handle my emotions?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
I understand — a rebellious child can wear a parent down emotionally. 🙏

**First, for your own heart** (this is what steadies everything else):

📿 **Heart Sutra** 3–7 times a day
Before reciting say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], to gain wisdom, keep a clear and calm mind, and remove my afflictions."*
(Not after 10pm)

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** 3–7 times a day
*"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], with good health and strengthened spiritual energy."*

**For your child:**

📿 **Heart Sutra** at least 7 times a day, recited for the child
*"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless [child's full name] to gain wisdom."*

📿 **Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots** 21 times a day
*"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva help me, [your full name], and [child's full name], to resolve our negative karmic affinity."*

⚠️ One important point from Master Lu: for a child who is stubborn or hard to discipline, **limit the Great Compassion Mantra recited for the child to 7 times per day** — reciting a large number can increase their energy and make them even harder to guide.

Master Lu's teaching on this:

> "First, you should not use an adult's way of thinking to restrain the innocent and playful nature of children."

He also explains that conflict between parent and child often comes from karmic conflicts of previous lives — which is why the Mantra to Untie Karmic Knots is used, rather than more arguing.

So the practice is: don't fight the child — soften the karmic knot, and pray for your own clarity. Keep reciting steadily.

May I ask — have you recited Buddhist scriptures before, or is this new to you? That way I can suggest the right starting point for you. 🙏

*Reference: Buddhism Q&A (Q127), Metaphysics Q&A Vol. 3 (Q114)*

═══ CHIP5-en I am new to 心灵法门,  — guard: clean ═══
Q: I am new to 心灵法门, what is the first step?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 2 (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 1 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,introduction,qa_general
  ✓ non-trivial reply (≥120 chars)
  ✓ no blanket refusal tail
  ✓ not the safety hand-off
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Welcome 🙏 It's a good sign that you're asking.

The first step is simple — start chanting. Don't worry about doing everything at once.

**Start with these two:**

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra (Ta Pei Chou)** — 3 times a day
Before you begin, say:
*"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [say your full name], grant me good health and a peaceful mind."*

📿 **Heart Sutra (Hsin Ching)** — 3 times a day
Before you begin, say:
*"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [say your full name], grant me wisdom, a clear and calm mind, and free me from worries."*
(Please don't recite the Heart Sutra after 10pm.)

**When you finish**, simply say:
*"Thank you, Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, for protecting and blessing me, [full name]."*

That's it. That's your whole practice for now.

**If you don't know how to pronounce the words** — that's completely fine. There are follow-along chanting videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Just chant along with the video. Many people start this way.

**A few things to keep in mind:**
- Consistency matters more than quantity. 3 times every day is better than 21 times once and then stopping.
- Master Lu taught that the Great Compassion Mantra can be recited 3 or 7 times daily throughout one's whole life — it's a foundation, not a temporary fix.
- Once these two feel comfortable (usually after a week or two), you can add the Eighty-eight Buddhas Great Repentance — but start with just 1 time. No need to rush.

Everything in Guan Yin Citta is **completely free** — books, chanting materials, guidance. Nobody should ever charge you for anything.

Keep going, and the mind will slowly settle 🙏

May I ask — is there something specific going on in your life right now that brought you here? Health, family, work? That way I can suggest something more suited to your situation.

